# README screenshots

After meaningful UI/copy/visual changes, refresh product screenshots instead of capturing them ad hoc in chat.

1. Ensure the app is serving locally: `npm run dev` (default `http://127.0.0.1:4173`).
2. Run: `npm run shots` (= `node scripts/capture-readme-shots.mjs`).
3. Override URL if needed: `PWA_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4173 npm run shots`.
4. Output:
   - `docs/screenshots/01-…08-….png` — onboarding, today, waiting, answers, garden, history, plus, settings
   - `docs/screenshots/new/*` — ours, lists, moments, share, pair-code, etc.
5. Include updated PNGs in the same commit as the UI change when screenshots are part of the deliverable.

Do not invent a parallel capture flow unless the existing script is broken; fix `scripts/capture-readme-shots.mjs` instead.
